## Errors & Mistakes
The initial osascript implementation displayed a banner but sent clicks to Script Editor. The first terminal-notifier request failed with "Could not request notification permission: Notifications are not allowed for this application". Registering the Homebrew application bundle with Launch Services allowed macOS to request permission. The installer now performs that registration.

## Dead Ends
Herdr rejected importing the stock toast from outside the custom mod directory, including through a symlink to the stock module. The installer copies the bundled toast into the custom mod so the wrapper can inherit its in-app behavior.

## Hints for Future Agents
Herdr's built-in agent alerts carry the agent.focus action and its target terminal address. Keep that address with the individual notification because another agent can become active before the user clicks. The click command runs through /bin/sh with its own environment. Quote the arguments and pass the app home explicitly.

## Codebase Discoveries
The desktop app uses the dotfiles-main layout. Its toast setting is independent of the TUI configuration. macOS attributes the banners to terminal-notifier. Herdr-generated editor files and the installed copy of the bundled toast are outside this commit.

